From: OrdinaryFun <ordinaryfun@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: drain RX retry before common CE cleanup

The RX replenishment retry callback can post buffers and rearm itself after
an allocation or DMA mapping failure. Stopping CE IRQ tasklets alone does
not drain this timer. Only native AHB stop currently deletes it; PCIC stop
and core crash reconfiguration enter common CE cleanup without doing so.
The callback can race RX buffer cleanup or survive into HAL ring reset.

Move the existing synchronous timer deletion into common CE cleanup,
before shadow timer and RX buffer cleanup. All callers must still quiesce
IRQ/tasklet producers first. This is a restartable stop, not permanent
timer shutdown: recovery reuses the timer without calling timer_setup().
The callback, posting fast path and successful native AHB stop order are
unchanged. This does not fix QMI_FAIL partial remove or prove that every
hybrid recovery caller already quiesces all CE producers.

---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -426,6 +426,5 @@ static void ath11k_ahb_stop(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	ath11k_ahb_ce_irq_disable_sync(ab);
-	timer_delete_sync(&ab->rx_replenish_retry);
 	ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes(ab);
 }
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
@@ -889,6 +889,8 @@ void ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	struct ath11k_ce_pipe *pipe;
 	int pipe_num;
 
+	/* IRQ/tasklet producers must already be quiesced by the caller. */
+	timer_delete_sync(&ab->rx_replenish_retry);
 	ath11k_ce_stop_shadow_timers(ab);
 
 	for (pipe_num = 0; pipe_num < ab->hw_params.ce_count; pipe_num++) {
